cue0009316
01:23:46.554 --> 01:24:01.754
And for them it's... That's what Hakhamim said. For you maybe is to be a lawyer or an accountant or an architect or whatever it is.

cue0009317
01:24:01.754 --> 01:24:08.754
Sages are the same. You have to be a Melechah which is simple for you and clean for you.

cue0009318
01:24:08.754 --> 01:24:17.754
Some people, for them to be a Melechah is a mess, a mess, and not a mess.

cue0009319
01:24:17.754 --> 01:24:22.754
For other people it is, it depends on what you want to do. You have to make your choices.

cue0009320
01:24:22.754 --> 01:24:28.754
The point of the Gemara here is in not giving you a geometrical answer.

cue0009321
01:24:28.754 --> 01:24:36.754
That's the sophistication of the Gemara. There are no geometrical things because there are no geometrical people.

cue0009322
01:24:36.754 --> 01:24:47.754
But within all of these three scenarios, or possible scenarios, shouldn't all of them have a common theme of trying to always increase your capacity for learning?

cue0009323
01:24:47.754 --> 01:25:10.368
Well I don want to say something very important Learning has nothing to do with quantity There is a very beautiful teshuba I mentioned many times of Rabbi Yaaqob Bera And Rabbi Yaaqob Bera was one of the finest Tamiyah Hakhamim at the time of the Gerush the teacher of Maran Qadosh

cue0009324
01:25:10.368 --> 01:25:21.688
